{
  "name": "01 - Intake / SMS Import",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "node-0003",
      "name": "Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        240,
        -220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## SMS Import (per-user relay)\n\nSingle Responsibility: webhook entrypoint for any SMS-forwarding tool (e.g. MacroDroid, Tasker, an iPhone Shortcut, a Twilio inbound webhook) that posts a raw SMS into this n8n instance. Checks a secret header, normalizes the payload, filters out obvious non-transaction messages (OTPs, promos), then relays the message straight to the app's own /api/imports/sms endpoint — which does the actual parsing, categorization, dedup, and confidence scoring (same engine used by the Telegram bot and iOS Shortcut integrations).\n\nSECURITY (two independent checks):\n  1. Transport secret — header `X-BudgetFlow-Webhook-Secret` must match the `N8N_SMS_WEBHOOK_SECRET` n8n environment variable. Proves the request came through our trusted relay pipeline. Missing/mismatched → HTTP 401 before anything else runs.\n  2. Per-user identity — the caller must also forward an `Authorization: Bearer bf_import_...` header carrying THAT USER'S OWN import token (Settings → Generate Token, self-serve). This workflow does not validate that token itself — it's forwarded unchanged to /api/imports/sms, which resolves it to a userId. This is what makes the workflow multi-tenant: one shared workflow for everyone, with per-user identity carried by the request rather than baked into the workflow or an n8n env var.\n\nNON-TRANSACTION FILTER: messages matching common OTP/promo phrasing (otp, one time password, verification code, do not share, login code, promotional offer) are recognized after normalization and short-circuited straight to a 200 `{ ok: true, ignored: true, reason: \"not_a_transaction\" }` response — they never reach the API.\n\nExpected POST body (once authenticated): { from?: string, body: string, receivedAt?: ISOString }. Adjust 'Normalize Payload' if your SMS forwarder uses different field names (e.g. Twilio sends { From, Body }).\n\nWebhook URL (after import, self-hosted): <your-n8n-instance>/webhook/budgetflow/sms-import",
        "height": 460,
        "width": 600,
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-0004",
      "name": "SMS Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        240,
        280
      ],
      "webhookId": "node-0005",
      "parameters": {
        "path": "budgetflow/sms-import",
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-0009",
      "name": "Check Secret",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        520,
        280
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "node-0010",
              "leftValue": "={{ $env.N8N_SMS_WEBHOOK_SECRET }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "notEmpty"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "node-0011",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.headers['x-budgetflow-webhook-secret'] }}",
              "rightValue": "={{ $env.N8N_SMS_WEBHOOK_SECRET }}",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-0012",
      "name": "Format 401 Response",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        800,
        460
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "manual",
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "node-0013",
              "name": "ok",
              "type": "boolean",
              "value": "={{ false }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "node-0014",
              "name": "error",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Unauthorized"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-0015",
      "name": "Respond 401",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        1080,
        460
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ $json }}",
        "options": {
          "responseCode": 401
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-0006",
      "name": "Normalize Payload",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        800,
        100
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "jsCode": "const item = ($input.first() && $input.first().json) || {};\nconst b = item.body || {};\nconst headers = item.headers || {};\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    source: \"SMS\",\n    rawText: b.body || b.Body || b.text || \"\",\n    chatId: null,\n    senderHint: b.from || b.From || null,\n    receivedAt: b.receivedAt || new Date().toISOString(),\n    // Per-user import token, forwarded unchanged to /api/imports/sms.\n    // The caller (iPhone Shortcut, forwarding app, etc.) sets this to\n    // THEIR OWN bf_import_... token, obtained from Settings.\n    authHeader: headers['authorization'] || headers['Authorization'] || null,\n  },\n}];"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-0016",
      "name": "Filter Non-Transaction",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1080,
        280
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "jsCode": "const input = ($input.first() && $input.first().json) || {};\nconst text = (input.rawText || \"\").toLowerCase();\n\n// EDIT ME: add more non-transaction phrases as you encounter them.\nconst ignorePatterns = [\n  \"otp\",\n  \"one time password\",\n  \"one-time password\",\n  \"verification code\",\n  \"do not share\",\n  \"login code\",\n  \"promotional offer\",\n];\n\nconst isIgnorable = ignorePatterns.some((p) => text.includes(p));\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    ...input,\n    isIgnorable,\n  },\n}];"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-0017",
      "name": "Is Ignorable?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        1360,
        280
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "node-0018",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.isIgnorable }}",
              "rightValue": true,
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-0019",
      "name": "Format Ignored Response",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        1640,
        380
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "manual",
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "node-0020",
              "name": "ok",
              "type": "boolean",
              "value": "={{ true }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "node-0021",
              "name": "ignored",
              "type": "boolean",
              "value": "={{ true }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "node-0022",
              "name": "reason",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "not_a_transaction"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-0023",
      "name": "Respond Ignored",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        1920,
        380
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ $json }}",
        "options": {
          "responseCode": 200
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-0007",
      "name": "Forward to Import API",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        1640,
        100
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $env.BUDGETFLOW_BASE_URL + '/api/imports/sms' }}",
        "authentication": "none",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "Authorization",
              "value": "={{ $json.authHeader }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "sendQuery": false,
        "options": {
          "timeout": 15000,
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "neverError": true,
              "responseFormat": "json",
              "fullResponse": true
            }
          }
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ ({ \"sender\": ($json.senderHint), \"message\": ($json.rawText), \"receivedAt\": ($json.receivedAt) }) }}"
      },
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 3,
      "waitBetweenTries": 2000,
      "continueOnFail": true,
      "alwaysOutputData": true
    },
    {
      "id": "node-0008",
      "name": "Respond",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        1920,
        100
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ $json.body }}",
        "options": {
          "responseCode": "={{ $json.statusCode || 200 }}"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
